  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Only in&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0dabeb1a-fc69-4272-a42a-af522ecbe520-image.png\" style=\"width: 149px; height: 107px;\" />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;can be substituted by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;combine with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;to form a yellow precipitate&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgI</mi></math>. While</p><p>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>II</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi></math> substitution reaction is not possible due to partial double bond character.</p>",
